#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: Montana
#> pause: 50
#> must: Iowa
#> must: Kansas
#> must: Montana
#> not: Alabama
#> not: Texas
#> source: x;/Iowa/!d
# 20. Print the paragraph that contains a word. Pement: sed -e '/./{H;$!d;}' -e 'x;/AAA/!d;'
# Paragraphs are separated by blank lines. Every non-blank line is appended
# to the hold space (H) and deleted. At a blank line (or the last line) x
# swaps the collected paragraph in; it is deleted unless it mentions Iowa.
# The blank line itself is now in the hold space, ready to start the next one.
# Try: /Iowa\|Ohio/!d  prints two of the three paragraphs.
/./{H;$!d;}
x;/Iowa/!d

#DATA
Alabama
Alaska

Iowa
Kansas
Montana

Ohio
Texas
